- `defines(v1, ...)`, `defines(v2, ...)`, `defines(v3, ...)`, `defines(v4, ...)`, `defines(v5, ...)`: Ranges are empty `{}`, failing to reflect the binary value spaces required by source decisions like "is the mailbox empty?" and "is the information complete?" (SMC6).
- `guard` statements (all): Entirely absent; source conditionals ("if not, continue", "If it is empty, the process ends", "If it is complete", etc.) are not enforced on outgoing edges of `branch(b1, XOR)` through `branch(b5, XOR)` (SMC2, SMC4).
- `label(n2, n3, "No")`, `label(n4, n6, "No")`, `label(n7, n9, "No")`, `label(n12, n13, "No")`, `label(n14, n16, "No")`: Applied to linear precedence edges preceding decision points rather than branch outgoing edges, failing to annotate the actual choice outcomes specified in the source (SMC2, SMC4).
- `action(n10, "add incoming mail number date and record it in letter book")`: Lacks outgoing precedence after `branch(b3, XOR)`, creating a dead-end path that contradicts the source progression which expects the process to continue after recording data (SMC1, SMC4, SMC5).
- `action(n15, "skip taking letter book and member register")`: Lacks outgoing precedence after `branch(b4, XOR)`, terminating the flow when it is not Wednesday, whereas the source implies normal continuation (SMC1, SMC5).
- `precedence(n20, n21)` and `precedence(n21, n22)`: Chain "write the data", "calculate the fee", and "hand the letter to Charles" sequentially, directly contradicting the source instruction "Simultaneously, calculate the fee and hand the letter to Charles" which mandates concurrent execution (SMC4).
- `action(n27, "add new member to register")` and associated actions (`n26`, `n28`-`n30`): Incorrectly placed on the rejection branch following `branch(b5, XOR)` → `action(n18, "write to applicant and inform decision")`; the source associates registering members, invoicing, and handing letters to Charles with successful membership, not applicants who "cannot become a member" (SMC1, SMC3, SMC7).
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Assigns every node to a single generic actor, omitting explicit source responsibilities for "Miranda" (receives books/register) and "Charles" (writes register amounts, handles letters/cards) (SMC7).

Structural Check
- [S1] STC8 failed: Each action node must have exactly one incoming and one outgoing edge. | Node `n10` has in=1 and out=0. | Node `n15` has in=1 and out=0. | DSL: action(n10,"add incoming mail number date and record it in letter book"); action(n15,"skip taking letter book and member register")
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v4` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v5` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n5` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n7` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b2 -> n8` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n10` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b3 -> n11` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n14` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n15` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b5 -> n17` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b5 -> n18` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.
- [S4] STC20 failed: Every non-end node must have a path to at least one end node. | Violations: n10, n15 | DSL: action(n10,"add incoming mail number date and record it in letter book"); action(n15,"skip taking letter book and member register")